member.summary:
Diagnostic (J-dump): per-node form-restoring force (body frame, N) from the last substep.
            Outward when relieving an over-deep panel, inward (shortening) when restoring an over-flat one;
            ~zero at the design shape. Node 0 (clew) and node N (head) are pinned, so always zero.

Finite-wing 3D lift-curve slope (per radian).
            a_3D = 2π · AR / (AR + 2). For AR=∞ this is 2π; for AR=4 it's ≈4.19;
            for AR=2 it's ≈3.14.

member.param:
Acute folded angle asin(SinAlpha) ∈ [0, π/2]. Non-negative;
            what the SAIL consumes for luff/stall thresholds. For a signed full-range angle (foil) use
